<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free State of Mecklenburg-Strelitz</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1934 CE · capital Neustrelitz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Smallest north German republic of the Weimar era, the successor of the grand duchy, merged with its neighbour by the Nazis.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolphus-frederick-vi-grand-duke-of-mecklenburg-strelitz">Grand Duke Adolf Frederick VI</a> died in February 1918 without a direct heir, leaving the throne in dispute. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-revolution-of-1918-1919">November revolution</a> a state council took over, and Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a> became a free state, adopting a constitution in 1919 and ending the archaic feudal constitution of 1755.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The free state was a parliamentary republic with a Landtag elected by universal suffrage, governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neustrelitz">Neustrelitz</a>. It remained rural, poor and sparsely populated, with large estates, and included the detached district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratzeburg">Ratzeburg</a>. Its small size made it financially weak, and governments alternated between Social Democrats and conservative parties.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Nazi seizure of power the Landtag was dissolved. On 1 January 1934 a Reich law merged it with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-mecklenburg-schwerin">Free State of Mecklenburg-Schwerin</a> into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-mecklenburg">Free State of Mecklenburg</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/free-state-of-mecklenburg-strelitz.jpg" alt="Free State of Mecklenburg-Strelitz" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Gro%C3%9Fherzogt%C3%BCmer_Mecklenburg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1934 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Neustrelitz</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Freistaat Mecklenburg-Strelitz</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1926&amp;focus=free-state-of-mecklenburg-strelitz" aria-label="Free State of Mecklenburg-Strelitz on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4971 342 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free State of Mecklenburg-Strelitz lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5291 598L5291 598M5291 598L5300 622M5291 598L5254 591"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5291 598h0M5300 622h0M5254 591h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5291 598h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5291 598h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Neustrelitz. <a href="/atlas?year=1926&amp;focus=free-state-of-mecklenburg-strelitz">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
